MewStage vendor patch text/0002 (third_party/NOTICE): the half-leading of a line box may be negative, as in CSS. A
paragraph LineHeight below the text's own height (a display face at line-height .85) now centres the text on the
line box with equal overhang; clamping at zero pushed it down by half the difference. Without a paragraph
LineHeight the line box is never smaller than the text, so default layout is unchanged.

--- a/Text/ManagedTextEngine.cs
+++ b/Text/ManagedTextEngine.cs
@@ -337,9 +337,13 @@
     /// Splits the room a line box has beyond the text's own ascent and descent evenly above and below it,
     /// the way a CSS line box does. Given to the descent side alone, a font with line gap - or a line
     /// height the paragraph set - holds its text against the top of the box.
+    /// MewStage vendor patch text/0002: the half-leading may be negative, as in CSS. A paragraph line height below the
+    /// text's own height (a display face at line-height .85) centres the text on the line box and lets its
+    /// ascent and descent overhang it equally; clamping at zero pushed the text down by half the difference.
+    /// Without a paragraph line height the line box is at least the text's height, so nothing changes there.
     /// </summary>
     private static double ApplyHalfLeading(double baseline, double lineHeight, double textHeight)
-        => baseline + (Math.Max(0, lineHeight - textHeight) / 2);
+        => baseline + ((lineHeight - textHeight) / 2);
 
